/-
# Maximal subquasivarieties of a finitely generated group (Kourovka Notebook Problem 14.25)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 14.25 (A. I. Budkin): let `qG` be the
quasivariety generated by a group `G`. Is there a finitely generated group `G` such that the set of
proper maximal subquasivarieties of `qG` is infinite?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Finiteness

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.QuasivarietyMaximalSubquasivarietiesKourovka14Problem25Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 14.25 (A. I.
Budkin). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701010 (`KOU-14.25`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Quasivarieties are the classes of groups defined by sets of quasi-identities `∀ x (w₁ = 1 ∧ ⋯ ∧ wₖ =
1 → w = 1)`, compared on groups in `Type` (a quasivariety is determined by its countable members).
`qG` is the class defined by all quasi-identities of `G` (Mal'cev). "Infinitely many" is "for every
`k`, `k` pairwise distinct ones".
-/

/-- **Quasi-identities of groups.** A quasi-identity in $n$ unknowns $x_0, \dots, x_{n-1}$ is a
formula $\forall x\,(w_1 = 1 \wedge \dots \wedge w_k = 1 \to w = 1)$, given by the number $n$, a
finite list of premises $w_1, \dots, w_k$ and a conclusion $w$, all of them elements of the free
group on $x_0, \dots, x_{n-1}$. -/
structure QuasiIdentity where
  /-- The number of unknowns. -/
  n : ℕ
  /-- The premises `w₁, …, wₖ`. -/
  premises : List (FreeGroup (Fin n))
  /-- The conclusion `w`. -/
  conclusion : FreeGroup (Fin n)

/-- **Quasi-identities holding in a group.** A quasi-identity
$\forall x\,(w_1 = 1 \wedge \dots \wedge w_k = 1 \to w = 1)$ in the unknowns $x_0, \dots, x_{n-1}$
holds in a group $G$ when every assignment of elements of $G$ to the unknowns under which each
premise $w_1, \dots, w_k$ evaluates to $1$ in $G$ also makes the conclusion $w$ evaluate to $1$. -/
def QuasiIdentity.HoldsIn (q : QuasiIdentity) (G : Type*) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∀ x : Fin q.n → G, (∀ w ∈ q.premises, FreeGroup.lift x w = 1) →
    FreeGroup.lift x q.conclusion = 1

/-- **The quasivariety defined by a set of quasi-identities.** For a set $Q$ of quasi-identities,
a group $H$ belongs to the quasivariety defined by $Q$ when every quasi-identity in $Q$ holds in
$H$. Every quasivariety of groups has this form.

Only groups in the lowest universe are considered; a quasivariety is determined by its countable
members. -/
def Models (Q : Set QuasiIdentity) (H : Type) [Group H] : Prop :=
  ∀ q ∈ Q, q.HoldsIn H

/-- **The quasi-identities of a group.** The quasi-theory of a group $G$ is the set of all
quasi-identities that hold in $G$. The quasivariety defined by this set is the quasivariety $qG$
generated by $G$. -/
def quasiTheory (G : Type) [Group G] : Set QuasiIdentity :=
  {q | q.HoldsIn G}

/-- **Inclusion of quasivarieties.** For sets $Q_1$ and $Q_2$ of quasi-identities, the
quasivariety defined by $Q_1$ is contained in the quasivariety defined by $Q_2$: every group in
which all quasi-identities of $Q_1$ hold also satisfies all quasi-identities of $Q_2$.

Only groups in the lowest universe are considered; a quasivariety is determined by its countable
members. -/
def QVLe (Q₁ Q₂ : Set QuasiIdentity) : Prop :=
  ∀ (H : Type) [Group H], Models Q₁ H → Models Q₂ H

/-- **Maximal proper subquasivarieties.** Let $G$ be a group and let $qG$ be the quasivariety
generated by $G$, that is, the quasivariety defined by the set of all quasi-identities that hold in
$G$. A set $Q$ of quasi-identities defines a maximal proper subquasivariety of $qG$ when the
quasivariety defined by $Q$ is contained in $qG$ but does not contain $qG$, and every quasivariety
$V$ defined by a set of quasi-identities with $V$ containing the quasivariety defined by $Q$ and
contained in $qG$ either is contained in the quasivariety defined by $Q$ or contains $qG$. -/
def IsMaximalProperSubquasivariety (G : Type) [Group G] (Q : Set QuasiIdentity) : Prop :=
  QVLe Q (quasiTheory G) ∧ ¬ QVLe (quasiTheory G) Q ∧
    ∀ Q' : Set QuasiIdentity, QVLe Q Q' → QVLe Q' (quasiTheory G) →
      QVLe Q' Q ∨ QVLe (quasiTheory G) Q'

/-- **Budkin's problem on maximal subquasivarieties (Kourovka 14.25).** The statement that there
is a finitely generated group $G$ such that the quasivariety $qG$ generated by $G$ has infinitely
many maximal proper subquasivarieties: for every natural number $k$ there are sets of
quasi-identities $Q_0, \dots, Q_{k-1}$, each defining a maximal proper subquasivariety of $qG$,
such that for $i \ne j$ the quasivarieties defined by $Q_i$ and $Q_j$ are different. -/
def finitelyGeneratedGroupInfinitelyManyMaximalSubquasivarieties : Prop :=
  ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), Group.FG G ∧
    ∀ k : ℕ, ∃ Q : Fin k → Set QuasiIdentity, (∀ i, IsMaximalProperSubquasivariety G (Q i)) ∧
      ∀ i j, i ≠ j → ¬ (QVLe (Q i) (Q j) ∧ QVLe (Q j) (Q i))

/--
**Some finitely generated group has infinitely many maximal subquasivarieties.** There is a
finitely generated group $G$ such that the quasivariety $qG$ generated by $G$ has infinitely many
maximal proper subquasivarieties: for every natural number $k$ there are sets of quasi-identities
$Q_0, \dots, Q_{k-1}$, each defining a maximal proper subquasivariety of $qG$, such that for
$i \ne j$ the quasivarieties defined by $Q_i$ and $Q_j$ are different.

This answers Kourovka Problem 14.25 positively; the answer is due to Bludov.

Source: E. I.
Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st
issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 14.25 (A. I. Budkin);
resolution: V. V. Bludov, Algebra and Logic 41 (2002), no. 1, 1-8, Kourovka Archive, Problem 14.25
(answer: Yes, it is).
-/
public theorem_wanted finitelyGeneratedGroupInfinitelyManyMaximalSubquasivarieties_holds :
    finitelyGeneratedGroupInfinitelyManyMaximalSubquasivarieties

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.QuasivarietyMaximalSubquasivarietiesKourovka14Problem25Wanted
